he perimeter of its bounding box. An empty frame has exactly the perimeter count.\n\n**What happens to the other frames.** Their fate depends only on whether their bounding box has the same size as the template's box.\n\n| Pair | Template size | Same size (pattern copied in own colour) | Different size (erased to background) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | 6×5 | 3, 2, 4 | 7 (4×5) |\n| 2 | 7×8 | 6, 4 | 5 (5×5) |\n| 3 | 6×7 | 2, 1 | 7 (7×6, transposed size), 3 (4×4) |\n\nSo a matching frame gets the template pattern stamped at the same relative offsets, recoloured to the frame's own colour, and it is not rotated. A frame of any other size is deleted.\n\n**Applying it to the test.** The colour‑7 frame (5×8) holds the pattern.\n- Frames 5 and 1 are also 5×8, so each receives the pattern in its own colour.\n- Frames 8 (6×10), 3 (4×9) and 6 (6×6) do not match, so they are erased.\n\n**Teaching stages.** The program emits one checkpoint per frame it handles, either \"stamped\" or \"erased\". The last checkpoint is the final grid.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid)\n    bg = background(g)\n    out = g.copy()\n    frames = []\n    for c in np.unique(g):\n        if c == bg:\n            continue\n        ys, xs = np.where(g == c)\n        y0, x0, y1, x1 = ys.min(), xs.min(), ys.max(), xs.max()\n        h, w = y1 - y0 + 1, x1 - x0 + 1\n        perim = 2 * h + 2 * w - 4\n        frames.append((int(c), y0, x0, h, w, len(ys) > perim))\n    tmpl = [f for f in frames if f[5]][0]\n    tc, ty, tx, th, tw, _ = tmpl\n    mask = g[ty:ty + th, tx:tx + tw] == tc\n    for c, y0, x0, h, w, pat in frames:\n        if c == tc:\n            continue\n        if (h, w) == (th, tw):\n            region = out[y0:y0 + h, x0:x0 + w]\n            region[mask] = c\n            emit(out, f\"Frame of colour {c} has the template's size {h}x{w}: stamp the template pattern in colour {c}.\")\n        else:\n            out[out == c] = bg\n            emit(out, f\"Frame of colour {c} is {h}x{w}, not the template's {th}x{tw}: erase it.\")\n    emit(out, \"Final grid.\")\n    return out\n","candidate_tactics":{"selection":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"**What happens to the other frames.** Their fate depends only on whether their bounding box has the same size as the template's box."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"| Pair | Template size | Same size (pattern copied in own colour) | Different size (erased to background) |"}],"recolour":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"So a matching frame gets the template pattern stamped at the same relative offsets, recoloured to the frame's own colour, and it is not rotated."}],"rigid":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"| 3 | 6×7 | 2, 1 | 7 (7×6, transposed size), 3 (4×4) |"}],"template":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"I find the template as the colour whose cell count is larger than the perimeter of its bounding box."},{"source":"final explanation","text":" the other frames.** Their fate depends only on whether their bounding box has the same size as the template's box."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"| Pair | Template size | Same size (pattern copied in own colour) | Different size (erased to background) |"}],"topology":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Exactly one frame is different: its interior also contains a pattern drawn in the frame's colour."}],"count":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"I find the template as the colour whose cell count is larger than the perimeter of its bounding box."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"An empty frame has exactly the perimeter count."}],"crop":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"I find the template as the colour whose cell count is larger than the perimeter of its bounding box."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"**What happens to the other frames.** Their fate depends only on whether their bounding box has the same size as the template's box."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_d